<title>USA: News anchor quits Chicago NBC-TV station - report.</title>
<headline>News anchor quits Chicago NBC-TV station - report.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>News anchor Ron Magers said Friday he was quitting the local NBC-TV outlet, two weeks after his co-anchor Carol Marin resigned over news values at the station that hired a talk-show host to do commentary.</p>
<p>Magers, speaking to WBBM-Radio in Chicago, said his last broadcast on WMAQ-TV would be Wednesday, May 21, but that he hoped to remain in Chicago.</p>
<p>Marin's resignation, triggered by the hiring of former news anchor and tabloid talk-show host Jerry Springer, touched off public moralizing about the state of television news. Springer did only two commentaries before quitting.</p>
</text>
